{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1426917-pre-nova-era-colonies","id":1426917,"title":"Pre-Nova era colonies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-12-01T21:57:22-08:00","id":1426917,"title":"Pre-Nova era colonies","content":"I'm playing around with an idea for a product for a trinity era &quot;lost colony&quot;, but it turns on one thing--the idea that the Doyen or another group might have transported humans to another world <i>before</i> the Nova era. The Doyan were active after the Hammersmith event, but it's confirmed that there were other alien influence on earth before the Nova era, correct?<br /> <br /> The time period for the kidnap/transfer would have been the late 19th/early 20th centuries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-01T22:40:28-08:00","id":1426923,"title":"","content":"Well, this one is a tonne of fun. I think that they could worship the Doyen as gods - if they know about them - and possibly believe that they're - both colonists and Doyen - Earth's salvation. I'm not sure which version of &quot;punk&quot; their technology but some kind of psi-punk may be pretty neat. Perhaps they surveil / put sleeper cells into Terran society starting only a generation or so after the era of the Grand Abduction (perhaps they have a cool name for it with biblical overtones a la The Ascension). Could be adversaries in the Adventure, Core, Aberrant and Aeon eras all the way. <br /> <br /> There's a parallel reality in the comic series The Authority called Sliding Albion about these blue-skinned humanoids whose dominant culture is really similar to a high-tech version of the Victorian-era British Empire. This kind of reminds me of that. If it were 19th Century, the British, German and Russian Empires were fairly ascendant and could possibly dominate the growth path of the Doyen colony (think lots of impractical headwear).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7165-queen-anne-country","name":"Queen Anne Country","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-01T23:04:39-08:00","id":1426926,"title":"","content":"They definitely make it clear that there were alien contacts with humanity before the nova era, and that there are more aliens than just those detailed so far in the books. So, yes, this absolutely fits into the game and it's one of the plots I've been considering too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T02:11:03-08:00","id":1426935,"title":"","content":"It would give a kind of StarGate feeling, lacking the StarGate per se.<br /> <br /> The Psions are exploring and find a colony of humans with some weird technology.<br /> They are certain the tech would be Nova Tech, but it\u2019s psi, and not biotech, it\u2019s based in crystals, much similar to the ones Clairs use.<br /> When they arrive to talk, the people treat them as gods, as they have the powers the gods manifest.<br /> <br /> The alien can be a parasite like Goa\u2019uld (from StarGate), occupying the body of the \u201cpriests\u201d to interact with the population, and capable of using their original powers from inside, I would not make them live all the time inside people, just to interact with the humans. Or they can be a more traditional alien (non parasite) that have Psionic powers and are worshiped by the population.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T02:48:52-08:00","id":1426942,"title":"","content":"A lot of how the plot goes might depend on why the aliens did the abduction. Research? Labor? Some religious purpose of their own? Sleeper agents for later planetary infiltration?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T14:24:37-08:00","id":1427037,"title":"","content":"Given that you apparently need psions or novas if you want an FTL drive, the alien abductors would probably have to either be psions/novas, or have reverse engineered FTL craft made by psions/novas. Either way, they probably possess some degree of very advanced tech.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T14:35:28-08:00","id":1427040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shalmaneser</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1426917-pre-nova-era-colonies?p=1426942#post1426942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of how the plot goes might depend on why the aliens did the abduction. Research? Labor? Some religious purpose of their own? Sleeper agents for later planetary infiltration?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure!<br /> <br /> One unusual reason could be an Interplanetary Zoo with species of many different planets.<br /> But the Zoo had to close (didn't profit properly or suffered from &quot;under developed species activists&quot; that forced the zoo to close) and the creatures had to be returned to their home planets.<br /> But in the end, their version of prime directive forced them to leave the humans in a different planet to avoid corrupting our culture (or the ones returning were just lazy and dropped the colony somewhere that they could live).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T16:36:02-08:00","id":1427055,"title":"","content":"For this, when/if I do it, I'm leaning towards: &quot;Friendly/neutral Doyen&quot; or simply unknown. This would avoid putting the GM in a corner, and introducing another species.<br /> The unknown could simply be: Okay, some hero/wanderer brought most of us here, displaying powerful noetic abilities, which could mean that he was possible a one in a million mutation...or possibly an alien wearing a human suit. <br /> <br /> The big thing for this would be the idea of a culture that has been influenced by talents and psi, and yet hasn't been in contact with earth since say, 1900. <br /> <br /> Psiads and Talents would be the dominant types, (I was considering having some &quot;mutant&quot; psions, but decided against it--if theDoyen had to go to all the trouble they did to create psions, its' highly unlikely any set of circumstances would allow them to develop 'naturally'.<br /> <br /> I am on the fence about whether or not to include superiors. The aliens could have left devices or instructions behind, and superiors would fit the kind of &quot;planetary romance&quot; feel the planet would have. OTH, some might consider that stealing Japan's thunder. <br /> <br /> One certain thing: They've never encountered novas or aberrants--don't even know what they are. In addition, none of their psiads have access to anything other than the basic quantakenesis powers. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-04T14:47:38-08:00","id":1427302,"title":"","content":"All those people that disappeared in the bermuda triangle (strong flux zone) ended up transported to said world.<br /> <br /> The flux zone/portal was an alien experiment on their version of a teaser.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2421-cknight","name":"cKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-04T17:20:17-08:00","id":1427317,"title":"","content":"Why can't some Mad Scientist from The 30s create a portal to another world Go full on Flash Gordon. Hell maybe an alien Hammersmith experiment might drag people from earth Isekai style","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-04T19:35:12-08:00","id":1427322,"title":"","content":"Well for this--doylist, I want to do with the nexus storypath thing, and that means giving a variety of reasons so that you don't trap the players/GM. I've decided to have the &quot;official&quot; period of transfers be between 1809-1909, because that was a period where a lot of stuff was happening and given the technological level of the world, it was easier to explain people missing. i might have other groups appear later, but none near enough to the &quot;present&quot; time to be aware of Aberrants or psions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-04T22:35:41-08:00","id":1427332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1426917-pre-nova-era-colonies?p=1427037#post1427037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that you apparently need psions or novas if you want an FTL drive, the alien abductors would probably have to either be psions/novas, or have reverse engineered FTL craft made by psions/novas. Either way, they probably possess some degree of very advanced tech.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe the lost colony isn't so far that it requires FTL. The Hammersmith Event not only fluxified a lot of people, it did it to places as well. They just eventually faded back to normal over time in most cases. <br /> <br /> Picture a colony of humans abducted by a Pulp-era Martian civilization that didn't actually exist before the Hammersmith event, and that faded away (along with all evidence that it had existed) as the Event waned. The humans, poor bastards, are completely normal, but left trying to survive with less and less of the advanced Martian tech that kept them alive on Mars- eventually making something that sort of barely works from reverse-engineered Martian tech. <br /> <br /> So skip ahead to the Aeon era, when someone doing prospecting in a remote and otherwise uninteresting area of Mars (or a clairsentient happens to notice, or a telepath picks something up) finds a deep subsurface cavern with some very odd humans and even odder equipment in it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-04T23:52:37-08:00","id":1427335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1426917-pre-nova-era-colonies?p=1427322#post1427322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well for this--doylist, I want to do with the nexus storypath thing, and that means giving a variety of reasons so that you don't trap the players/GM. I've decided to have the &quot;official&quot; period of transfers be between 1809-1909, because that was a period where a lot of stuff was happening and given the technological level of the world, it was easier to explain people missing. i might have other groups appear later, but none near enough to the &quot;present&quot; time to be aware of Aberrants or psions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Hammersmith experiment.. and theoretically alien variants there of broke time. Its why you have in the 30s places you can find dinosaurs which won't be there later. Go nuts! Lost viking colony! The Real answer for what happened at Roanoak, The lost Legion!<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_High_Crusade\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_High_Crusade</a> That sounds like something a bunch of talents might pull offf..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-06T18:42:05-08:00","id":1427507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NewK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1426917-pre-nova-era-colonies#post1426917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The time period for the kidnap/transfer would have been the late 19th/early 20th centuries.</div> </div> </div> </div>What could be amusing is a light-speed limited transportation system like the one used by the Zeps could result in future folk discovering a bunch of kidnapped humans from a previous century *who just arrived* at their destination, a hundred light-years away. For them, no time has passed, as they feel like they were just whisked away by a bright light from the late 19th century (or whenever) 'a few minutes ago.' Or they arrived a few months or years before the were re-discovered by Psions from Earth, but still haven't had a century or more to change or develop into a proper 'colony,' and are still kind of stuck in the mindset of a bunch of horribly out of place turn-of-the-century folk.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23754,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23754-ian-turner","user":"Ian Turner","date":". 12-06-2020, 09:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23754-ian-turner","name":"Ian Turner","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-06T21:59:11-08:00","id":1427522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ian Turner</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1426917-pre-nova-era-colonies?p=1427507#post1427507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> but still haven't had a century or more to change or develop into a proper 'colony,' and are still kind of stuck in the mindset of a bunch of horribly out of place turn-of-the-century folk.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's probably their planet now, though. If 22nd century people set foot on it, <i>they're</i> the ones horribly out of place.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure how much fun a game based on themes of Colonialism would be, but if you have players whose first impulse is to bring the &quot;natives&quot; out of their turn-of-the-century mindsets whether they want their minds changed or not, you've got it. Bonus points if the planet happens to have lots of useful raw materials/alien tech to trade cheap modern gadgets for or just take.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26448-shalmaneser","name":"Shalmaneser","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T05:43:16-08:00","id":1427570,"title":"","content":"Try this one. Alien observers visit Earth in the Minoan period. Aware of what will happen with Santorini, the aliens kidnap multiple human groups from the Minoan culture before the volcano blows. The humans do fairly well on a Terraformed planet seeded with Earth life. The aliens find the human cultural adaptations to new environments fascinating. So they take other groups that seem destined to be wiped out like Norse Greenlanders or the passengers of sinking ships. <br /> <br /> The &quot;colonies&quot; could be on one or several world's. The Hammersmith incident could have driven the aliens off. Or they could have left earlier for other reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T17:07:03-08:00","id":1427649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1426917-pre-nova-era-colonies?p=1427570#post1427570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Try this one. Alien observers visit Earth in the Minoan period. Aware of what will happen with Santorini, the aliens kidnap multiple human groups from the Minoan culture before the volcano blows. The humans do fairly well on a Terraformed planet seeded with Earth life. The aliens find the human cultural adaptations to new environments fascinating. So they take other groups that seem destined to be wiped out like Norse Greenlanders or the passengers of sinking ships.<br /> <br /> The &quot;colonies&quot; could be on one or several world's. The Hammersmith incident could have driven the aliens off. Or they could have left earlier for other reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> or you could have Aegis era colonies! Imagine classical mythological world preserved..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T18:00:27-08:00","id":1427657,"title":"","content":"That's honestly be a lot of research to get right, especially for classical age origins, right now, I don't have access to those resources in a reliable enough way to get it done. <br /> <br /> BUT... If you are interested in it, there's a product: Elderitch skies and Elderitch Skies companion set in a future where the Cthulhu mythos are mixed with modern space exploration and treated more as &quot;uber advanced aliens&quot; rather than the horror beings Lovecraft made them (for example, the &quot;Great old ones&quot; are mostly failed attempts at transcendence. )<br /> <br /> The book however has a fairly late number of worlds where ancient humans were brought or travelled themselves and haven't contacted eartch since then, so you might want to mine it for ideas.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T20:36:10-08:00","id":1427672,"title":"","content":"Classical era societies, which would be more than 1500 years after the Minoans, could fit my original idea. Heck, the Trojan War was more than half a millennium after the Santorini eruption. Aegis would fit perfectly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T22:16:25-08:00","id":1427676,"title":"","content":"Minoan/Mycenean civilizations aren't entirely well understood today and seem to slot into in part the age of myth as the classical greeks saw it. WHich since Aegis is already playing lose with mythology(after all this isn't scion) slotting it into that era seems to work decently. Similarly you could pull much off with the Indus valley civilization","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T09:35:13-08:00","id":1427719,"title":"","content":"A culture developed from H. Erectus and/or other hominids would be fun to design.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T10:17:15-08:00","id":1427723,"title":"","content":"What about Doyen enemies? Or victims of the Doyen? This alien race grabbed some humans seeing that they have the potential to activate quantum abiltiies and then forcibly erupts them going &quot;Hey, if these quantum using people are here, then the Doyen will stay away. We have weapons to fight them with.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T10:50:30-08:00","id":1427728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1426917-pre-nova-era-colonies?p=1427723#post1427723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about Doyen enemies? Or victims of the Doyen? This alien race grabbed some humans seeing that they have the potential to activate quantum abiltiies and then forcibly erupts them going &quot;Hey, if these quantum using people are here, then the Doyen will stay away. We have weapons to fight them with.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like the idea of test subjects rebelling against the Doyen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T13:54:30-08:00","id":1427748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1426917-pre-nova-era-colonies?p=1427728#post1427728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I like the idea of test subjects rebelling against the Doyen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, so do I. They escaped the Doyen somehow and then used information about what the Doyen abhor/fear. Centering their research (or perhaps stealing it from the Doyen's own information) they then find some race that is primitive enough to not question their sudden gaining of godlike power and then BAM! The aliens have their own guard dogs from the Doyen.<br /> <br /> Depending on how far back in time this was, the humans could develop their technology in unique ways. As has been mentioned before, would the nova-tech resemble something steampunky? Maybe dieselpunk? Or perhaps nuclearpunk? The future is yours.<br /> <br /> I would love to explore this idea myself but I am currently working on a nine world system that is not at all inspired by the Norse worlds. Nope. Not. At. All. [*hides my copy of AC Valhalla that totally inspired the idea*]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T14:43:57-08:00","id":1427758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1426917-pre-nova-era-colonies?p=1427748#post1427748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, so do I. They escaped the Doyen somehow and then used information about what the Doyen abhor/fear. Centering their research (or perhaps stealing it from the Doyen's own information) they then find some race that is primitive enough to not question their sudden gaining of godlike power and then BAM! The aliens have their own guard dogs from the Doyen.<br /> Depending on how far back in time this was, the humans could develop their technology in unique ways. As has been mentioned before, would the nova-tech resemble something steampunky? Maybe dieselpunk? Or perhaps nuclearpunk? The future is yours.<br /> I would love to explore this idea myself but I am currently working on a nine world system that is not at all inspired by the Norse worlds. Nope. Not. At. All. [*hides my copy of AC Valhalla that totally inspired the idea*]</div> </div> </div> </div>Taking the human or hominid template and applying different environmental pressure can give you some really neat &quot;alien&quot; humans. Humans (or hominids) who have survived in different environments could get pretty interesting. <br /> <br /> For example, take this illustration by Charles Le Brun (1619 \u2013 1690) who blended animal and human features into startling images.<br /> <img src=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/-lxvKAl3K8yA/V4fBGCap2-I/AAAAAAABO7M/txjvZ6X95AM/charles-le-brun-physiognomic-heads-1%25255B11%25255D.jpg?imgmax=1600\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T16:36:42-08:00","id":1427770,"title":"","content":"In that vein, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Man_After_Man\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Man_After_Man</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T17:15:38-08:00","id":1427775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1426917-pre-nova-era-colonies?p=1427719#post1427719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A culture developed from H. Erectus and/or other hominids would be fun to design.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good call, the Aliens could easily be old enough to have taken samples of the remnant populations of Homo Erectus, as well as Neanderthals, the Hobbits, and the Desnovians. Heck, you could play with ideas like telepathic Neanderthals (a common Sci-fi trope once).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T17:48:42-08:00","id":1427782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1426917-pre-nova-era-colonies?p=1427770#post1427770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In that vein, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Man_After_Man\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Man_After_Man</a></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Absolutely. And I might also add the humanoid breeds in Jack Vance's The Dragon Masters. An excellent book for this concept.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.pinimg.com/564x/fb/74/12/fb7412dbc9bcc280c21a27c8715de8f6.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <span style=\"color:#111111\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Illustration By Jack Gaughan</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T18:48:01-08:00","id":1427792,"title":"","content":"Or Brun drawings are awesome. I am working on a supplement to Aeon that my idea is to run Thundercats-ish campaign, with cat people, reptile people, bird people, etc. but the rules would be based on what Reconstruir (BK and VK working together) and genetic engineering would be able to create by splicing people and animals.<br /> <br /> I am on a test phase but soon...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T20:26:36-08:00","id":1427802,"title":"","content":"Well, think about this:<br /> Some aliens go &quot;Hmmm, those bipedal ones. They seem to be the dominant life form of their planet. They certainly have managed to go into just about any climate on their planet. Let's grab a bunch of them and then also some other fauna and flora and then mix them together to see if we can't improve them?&quot;<br /> <br /> Or worse/better: &quot;Why don't we see if we can't add in a dash of them to some life forms on other planets and see what comes out the other side?&quot;<br /> <br /> After all, science is not about the eureka moments but more of &quot;Hmmmm, I wonder what would happen if....&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-11T21:15:10-08:00","id":1428149,"title":"","content":"Go full Atlantis.<br /> <br /> Height of Human Civilization so far - including Neanderthal, Denisovian and others -, psionic-intuitive development in all Bronze Age ways (let's call it, Crystal Age?), counter-acting quantum-based humans - or, Titans -, trying to heal, control or imprision them. Pretty much, Tragedy repeats itself.<br /> <br /> Disaster struck when, trying to manipulate all these extraordinaire forces, their beloved Atlantis was engulfed in a quantum-originated mishap, which transported the whole city/island/continent to another world - maybe even time; leaving behind the very stuff of legends. From the resulting wreckage of the experiment, the survivors found themselves having to start anew in an unknown world.<br /> <br /> What society Aeon Trinity Psions would meet? That's a game I'd love to play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>\u03a8</b></i> The Corps is Father. The Corps is Mother. <i><b>\u03a8</b></i>","edited":{"userid":26309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26309-al-bester","user":"Al Bester","date":". 12-12-2020, 12:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26309-al-bester","name":"Al Bester","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-12T05:21:21-08:00","id":1428173,"title":"","content":"These all sound like great ideas.<br /> <br /> What\u2019s a Denisovian?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}